The P1 cancellation finding is addressed in `03125e06`: managed npm installation now rethrows an aborted startup signal immediately after every cancellation-aware install/repair/sync boundary, before ordinary failure retry, quarantine, reconciliation, or result handling. The regression verifies the original abort reason, one install attempt, and no recovery artifact.

Proof added to the PR body includes the SIGTERM startup lease-release regression, all 78 managed npm install tests, a real foreground Gateway reaching `/healthz`, `/readyz`, and RPC health, and a real managed replacement trace where gateway-1 stopped/released ownership and gateway-2 reached `/readyz=200 ready=true` on the same isolated state.

@clawsweeper re-review

