- the managed proxy SIGTERM path now waits for the full Gateway startup cleanup gate before process exit, so the startup lease is released first;
- configured-plugin repair and plugin update/install fallback paths now preserve and rethrow startup cancellation instead of converting it into an ordinary update failure.

The PR body now includes focused regressions plus an actual managed Gateway sequence showing SIGTERM, lease release, replacement lease reacquisition, and replacement `/readyz=200` readiness against the same state directory.

CI exposed three mechanical omissions on the prior head; fixed in `ddf14ebf1db`:

- moved the recovery-plan contract to break the Madge cycle;
- removed/documented the two new type assertions for the assertion-safety ratchet; and
