Updated exact head to `661adfb529c26bdce2ab43b577d898bff8ffae4a` to address the shutdown-availability finding.

The Gateway now uses one ordered, bounded sequence:

1. abort system-agent work and give turn drains a 5-second grace;
2. dispose native agent harnesses with their existing 5-second grace;
3. only after successful harness disposal, delete system-agent bindings with a separate 5-second bound.

This removes both indefinite waits and cleanup/harness concurrency. If harness disposal itself does not complete, binding cleanup is not started against a possibly live harness.

Exact-head local proof:

- 76 focused engine/session-disposal/gateway-close tests passed;
- full `scripts/check-changed.mjs` gate passed;
- fresh P1 autoreview reported no accepted/actionable findings;
- regression test timed out at 2,000 ms with the prior unbounded normal path and passed in 73 ms on this head.

